  "query_preview": "(Today through Sunday)...\nIssued at 329 AM EDT Mon Oct 26 2026\n\nRather complex yet quasi-stagnant synoptic pattern over North \nAmerica throughout this weekend will feature broad cut-off H500 \ntrough over Pacific Northwest/BC and more progressive but overall \nretracted polar waves from interior Canada to New England.  Between \nthese northern features upper ridging will attempt to establish over \nthe majority of CONUS...yet will be dampened by at least a couple \nweaknesses lifting from southern High Plains to Great Lakes.  These \nless intense waves will combine with broadening surface high \npressure over the eastern US to advect fetch of Gulf moisture from \nsouthern Plains to near IA/IL.\n\nThis will translate to much of the same conditions recently seen \nacross central Indiana...rain-free weather under generally stacked \nhigh pressure through Wednesday...as readings ranging from the 40s/ \naround 50F to afternoons peaking near 70-75F.  Remnant surface high \ncentered to our southeast will be replaced by stronger air mass \ncrossing Ontario into Tuesday...that will ultimately set up in the \nsame general proximity over the country's eastern third by Tuesday \nnight, albeit now with a seasonably strong gradient.  Therefore \nexpect typical October breeze finally returning to central Indiana \nfor Wednesday/Thursday afternoons...when south-southwesterly gusts \nto 10-20 mph will yield highs in the mid-/upper 70s, respectively.\n(Thursday's record high at Indianapolis is 81, 1922).  Considerable \ncloudiness also expected late Tuesday-early Wednesday from first, \nsmaller southern wave lifting to our west...with high confidence dry \ncolumn will continue dry conditions.\n\nSecond, broader weakness lifting across region this weekend will \nbring moderate certainty in scattered/numerous rain showers... \nassuming northern stream wave dives far enough south near Cape Cod \nto provide downstream confluence and prolong advection of better \nGulf moisture north of the Ohio Valley around the Saturday night to \nSunday timeframe.  Timing of onset of showers would likely be around \nHalloween evening...although more organized rain coverage would be \nfavored towards Sunday.  Indianapolis is progged for a streak of 13 \nconsecutive days with highs in the 70s through November 1st.  The \nnormal max/min at Indianapolis through the forecast period falls \nfrom 61/42 today...to 58/40 on Sunday.",
